From: Clemens Famulla-Conrad <cfamullaconrad@suse.com>
Subject: [PATCH] D-Bus: Drop leftover <allow send_interface="..."/> for root

Commit df9e2c2a55ee removed <deny send_interface="fi.w1.wpa_supplicant1"/>
from the default context but kept the matching allow rule for root, which
has had no purpose since.

Fixes: df9e2c2a55ee ("D-Bus: Don't do <deny send_interface="..." /> in dbus service file")

---
 wpa_supplicant/dbus/dbus-wpa_supplicant.conf |    1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

--- a/wpa_supplicant/dbus/dbus-wpa_supplicant.conf
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/dbus/dbus-wpa_supplicant.conf
@@ -6,7 +6,6 @@
                 <allow own="fi.w1.wpa_supplicant1"/>
 
                 <allow send_destination="fi.w1.wpa_supplicant1"/>
-                <allow send_interface="fi.w1.wpa_supplicant1"/>
                 <allow receive_sender="fi.w1.wpa_supplicant1" receive_type="signal"/>
         </policy>
         <policy context="default">
